// Architecture of the incremental bounded proof search implemented in src/search.
// Validate this design with:
// cargo run --release -- examples/proof-search-incremental.stypes --max-steps 10000000
//
// The logical interfaces below describe data flow, not a required Rust representation.
// Store IDs remain stable; ownership, borrowing, and mutation are implementation choices.
// Loops and dispatch are explicit operations: STN does not infer effect sequencing.
//
// Design invariants:
// - Search only DEFINITIONS; FEATURES are goals and never become available morphisms.
// - Preserve the relevant/exhaustive universes and inference rules from doc.md.
// - Minimize (primitive occurrences, inference occurrences) lexicographically.
// - Count occurrences in the unfolded proof tree, even when storage shares DAG nodes.
// - A smaller concrete universe provides witnesses, not global lower bounds.
// - Unknown heuristic cases use a zero function-count bound, never an unsupported positive estimate.
// - New types/rules may improve old pairs; processed pairs are not permanently closed.
// - Failure requires complete universe generation and proof saturation.
//
// Research basis: weighted AND/OR derivations and admissible abstractions.
// https://home.ttic.edu/~dmcallester/jair07.pdf
// https://cs.uky.edu/~sgware/reading/papers/bonet2001planning.pdf
// This first design uses conservative incremental relaxation. A*LD-style context
// estimates can later improve scheduling without changing certification contracts.

DEFINITIONS:

/// Checked declarations, owning semantic types, ground primitives, ordered ground goals,
/// source metadata, and the tuple-arity bound inferred during elaboration.
Specification

/// Validated profile, intermediate-depth and tuple-arity bounds, type/work limits,
/// and the positive alternative cap. The cap remains applicable to every type pair.
ValidationOptions

SearchRequest = (Specification, ValidationOptions)

/// Stable identifier of an interned semantic type; allocation does not admit it to search.
TypeId

/// Stable identifier of an original typed witness in the shared proof DAG.
ProofId

/// Canonical composition key using exactly the equivalences in doc.md section 8.1.
NormalFormId

/// Ground goal endpoints; its source declaration and substitutions remain in the plan.
GroundGoal = (TypeId, TypeId)

/// Nonnegative number of primitive occurrences in an unfolded proof tree.
FunctionCount

/// Nonnegative number of inference occurrences in an unfolded proof tree.
InferenceCount

Cost = (FunctionCount, InferenceCount)

/// A certified lexicographic lower bound on the minimum cost in the full selected domain.
/// A function-only lower bound L can safely become (L, 0).
/// For L >= 1, binary/unary rules also imply at least L - 1 inference occurrences.
CostBound = Cost

/// Resource counters shared by initialization, heuristic construction, generation,
/// rule activation, normalization, propagation, certification, and witness checking.
SearchUsage

/// Type capacity or work budget exhausted; includes the stage and consumed counters.
SearchLimit

/// Immutable definition of the complete selected search domain and its lazy generators.
/// Relevant mode uses the existing elementary-transformation closure, not arbitrary tuples.
/// Exhaustive mode additionally enumerates bounded constructors and normalized nonempty sums.
/// Explicit shapes remain admitted regardless of synthesis depth; existential packages
/// have no implicit packing/unpacking rules, and nominal construction remains forbidden.
/// Admission is decidable without first materializing every member of the domain.
UniversePlan

/// Small optimistic deduction model covering the full planned domain, including types
/// that have not yet been generated. Every concrete inference must have an abstract
/// simulation costing no more than it; relaxed paths are never emitted as witnesses.
/// First version: h_max for relevant domains containing only opaque types, products,
/// and nominal views, with zero-cost optimistic structural steps.
/// Any unsupported constructor anywhere in the domain, or the exhaustive profile,
/// disables positive function-count bounds. Use the universal proof bound (0,1) instead.
/// For (X,Y) -> Z, combine prerequisites with max, then add the primitive cost.
/// Do not sum independent component estimates: one producer can return both components.
/// A covered goal may have a cheaper path through an uncovered rule; checking just
/// the goal's endpoints is insufficient to enable a positive estimate.
/// Require an admissibility argument for each supported rule before using a positive bound.
RelaxedModel

/// Cached certified lower bounds for all ground goals in the full selected domain.
/// Bounds depend on the plan and declarations, not on the currently generated subset.
LowerBounds:
    estimate: GroundGoal -> CostBound

/// Owning planning context: declarations, options, domain plan, lower bounds,
/// source metadata, and already charged usage. No concrete proof search has run yet.
SearchPlan:
    /// Admit explicit types and views, seed primitives and structural rules, and enqueue
    /// domain generators. Unsupported or expensive heuristic cases may use zero bounds.
    /// All admitted type IDs and original witness IDs are stable for the entire session.
    seed: () -> SearchState | SearchLimit

/// Consume the request, establish the domain plan, build a budgeted relaxed model,
/// and cache certified goal bounds. This stage does not eagerly close the concrete universe.
prepareSearch: SearchRequest -> SearchPlan | SearchLimit

/// One suspended finite-domain generator or one new type/context/elementary-transform join.
/// Its cursor records progress so resuming it does not rescan processed combinations.
TypeTask

/// Newly admitted types and elementary transformations; identities are deduplicated.
/// The owning state schedules their structural seeds and all newly applicable joins.
UniverseDelta

/// Generated prefix of the exact planned universe, owning type-admission membership,
/// pending generator cursors, and deduplicated elementary-transformation dependencies.
IncrementalUniverse:
    /// Perform one bounded generation batch. Relevant closure joins each new type/context
    /// with existing transforms, and each new transform with existing contexts, once.
    /// Exhaustive generation resumes constructor cursors subject to the original bounds.
    /// A derived general proof never enlarges the relevant profile's domain definition.
    expand: TypeTask -> UniverseDelta | SearchLimit

/// New endpoint, structural seed, or newly enabled inference relationship to index.
RuleTask

/// New inference relationships and seed witnesses enabled by admitted endpoints.
RuleDelta

/// Incremental indices for exact composition endpoints, same-input fanout branches,
/// admitted binary products, collection lifts, restrictions, sum extensions, and narrowing.
/// Deduplicate concrete relationships and join only newly available dependencies.
RuleIndex:
    /// Activate applicable relationships. If their premises already have witnesses,
    /// enqueue their conclusions immediately; do not wait for premises to change again.
    /// Admission and inference applicability use the unchanged rules from doc.md.
    activate: RuleTask -> RuleDelta | SearchLimit

/// A newly accepted original witness and the relationship updates it must trigger.
/// Queued references carry the pair's cost revision so stale work can be discarded safely.
ProofTask

/// Accepted cost improvements or new equal-cost normalized representatives, together
/// with the consequences and certification attempts that now need scheduling.
ProofDelta

/// Best currently known costs and up to the configured cap of original witnesses per pair.
/// Normalize only for deduplication; retain and charge the original checked witness tree.
/// A lower cost replaces the active representatives and advances the pair revision.
/// An equal cost is accepted only for a new normalized key while capacity remains.
/// Higher-cost witnesses and duplicates do not propagate. Old immutable DAG nodes remain
/// valid evidence even when their pair's active representatives have been replaced.
ProofRelation:
    /// Join the new witness with currently active premises through applicable rules.
    /// Composition adds child costs; fanout adds both branch costs; every inference adds one.
    /// Reopen every improved pair and propagate the improvement to its consequences.
    /// Equal-cost new representatives also propagate while respecting the per-pair cap.
    propagate: ProofTask -> ProofDelta | SearchLimit

/// A request to inspect one goal's best witnesses, full-domain lower bound,
/// retained normalized alternatives, and any available exhaustion evidence.
CertificationRequest
/// Checked original witnesses of equal minimum cost, with their goal and certificate.
CertifiedGoal
/// This goal has no derivation in the selected fully generated and saturated domain.
UnresolvableGoal
/// No certificate is available yet; valid provisional witnesses may still exist.
NotCertified
CertificationDecision = CertifiedGoal | UnresolvableGoal | NotCertified

/// Certificates relate witnesses to the full planned domain, never just the generated prefix.
CertificateChecker:
    /// Independently check candidate witnesses and their original costs.
    /// Certify a minimum when its full lexicographic cost equals a certified lower bound,
    /// or after full domain generation/activation, when all queued proof costs exceed
    /// every goal's best witness cost. Every inference costs strictly more than its premises.
    /// Function-count equality alone does not certify the inference-count tie breaker.
    /// Certify failure only at that full fixed point with no witness for the goal.
    certify: CertificationRequest -> CertificationDecision | SearchLimit

/// Reconsider a goal after a witness change, a stronger certified bound, or global exhaustion.
CertificateTask
/// Work shared across all goals. Every admitted delta schedules all consequences needed
/// for completeness; finishing a goal does not remove premises needed by other goals.
WorkItem = TypeTask | RuleTask | ProofTask | CertificateTask

/// Deterministic scheduling preference, not evidence that remaining proofs are expensive.
/// Order proof tasks by cost. Before generation completes, defer tasks whose cost exceeds
/// every goal bound: they cannot finish a goal early and new types may enable cheaper paths.
/// Periodically resume generators to avoid starvation, preserving expensive tasks for later.
/// Goal relevance may reorder work; it must not discard a task without a sound pruning argument.
WorkPriority

/// Pending generator, rule, proof, and certificate tasks with deduplication and resumable cursors.
/// Stable tie breaking follows declaration order and semantic structure, not hash iteration.
/// Empty proof work alone is not exhaustion: generation and activation must also finish.
WorkQueue:
    /// Assign a scheduling preference. In this first version, heuristic priorities are
    /// allowed to be inconsistent because improved pairs can be reopened.
    /// No minimum certificate is obtained merely by looking at the smallest queue priority.
    prioritize: WorkItem -> WorkPriority

/// Original typed proof DAG, normalized-key index, and an independent witness checker.
/// Search-local indices can be discarded after final roots have been selected.
ProofStore

/// Ordered per-goal records of provisional witnesses, certified minima, and alternatives.
/// A goal with a certified minimum is finished early once the alternative cap is filled.
/// If fewer alternatives are found, finish generation and propagate through all goal witness
/// costs. Pending strictly more expensive proofs cannot add another equal-cost alternative.
/// Goals lacking witnesses require full saturation before failure can be certified.
/// Already certified witnesses remain usable evidence; goal declarations never become primitives.
GoalProgress

/// Owning live session: plan, usage, incremental universe, rule index, proof relation,
/// work queue, proof store, goal progress, lower bounds, and certificate checker.
SearchState:
    /// If every goal is finished, return a completed search without generating unused types.
    /// Otherwise select a pending task, retaining the state with it in ReadyWork.
    /// When all work is exhausted, request final certification and finish only after
    /// every goal has a minimum certificate or a domain-relative failure certificate.
    /// A terminal outcome is wrapped in IterationResult, preserving counters and owned stores.
    next: () -> ReadyWork | IterationResult

    /// Explicit iterative driver: repeatedly call next and execute each ReadyWork,
    /// inspect the resulting IterationResult, and resume with its SearchState or return
    /// its completed/interrupted outcome. All context travels with the selected branch.
    /// This loop is implemented directly; its behavior is not inferred by STN.
    /// Finite admission, positive inference costs, best-cost replacement, and finite
    /// alternative caps ensure termination when resource limits allow full saturation.
    run: () -> CompletedSearch | InterruptedSearch

/// Owning result of one scheduler iteration, including the case where selection was terminal.
/// Its nominal distinction prevents identity or a full run from proving that this step ran.
IterationResult:
    /// Explicit outcome dispatch: expose the next loop state or the terminal owned session.
    inspect: () -> SearchState | CompletedSearch | InterruptedSearch

/// Selected task together with its owning state; dispatch retains all context across effects.
ReadyWork:
    /// Dispatch on WorkItem. Expand types, activate rules, propagate a witness, or certify a goal;
    /// apply the returned delta to the owning state and enqueue every newly enabled consequence.
    /// Stage-local SearchLimit becomes an interrupted IterationResult with the owned context.
    /// This operation includes explicit sum dispatch and context retention.
    execute: () -> IterationResult

/// Finished session with independently checked goal outcomes and complete ownership of evidence.
/// Completion means all requested goals are certified, not necessarily that the universe is full.
CompletedSearch
/// Interrupted session with counters, reason, owning stores, and provisional/certified progress.
/// First version preserves the current public behavior: interruption reports every goal
/// incomplete. Internally certified witnesses do not silently become an uncertified PROVED result.
InterruptedSearch

/// Final owning result compatible with the existing report pipeline: ordered goals/statuses,
/// options and tuple bound, type store, compacted original proof DAG, and usage counters.
SearchResult

/// Convert an initialization limit into the existing incomplete-result contract while retaining
/// all ground goal metadata and options needed for the report, even before the session exists.
/// SearchLimit carries this reporting context whenever it escapes preparation or seeding.
preparationFailed: SearchLimit -> InterruptedSearch

/// Explicit outcome dispatch. Preserve certificates and statuses on completion; on interruption
/// produce incomplete statuses. Select final roots, compact the DAG, and discard transient indices.
/// Every unit of final checking/compaction work is budgeted; exhaustion yields an incomplete result.
finishSearch: CompletedSearch | InterruptedSearch -> SearchResult

FEATURES:

/// Plan and seed a search without materializing the full concrete universe.
initializeSearch: SearchRequest -> SearchState | InterruptedSearch

/// One complete scheduler iteration, carrying completion/interruption without losing context.
advanceSearch: SearchState -> IterationResult

/// Consume the checked specification and options and produce the existing owning search result.
/// Errors in parsing/elaboration occur before this input; resource exhaustion is a result status.
search: SearchRequest -> SearchResult
